# Round glmpaper-replay's correction of glmrescli's card: GLM-5.3-Flash's decode under adaptive residency on
# plan (a) (A6000), the same binary, BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY unset (off) against mid-p0-s1 (0 pinned, 1 spare).
# The replay (glmreplay/glmreplay.py over the ik router set glm5next-prose, 24 contexts of 2048, 512 prompt
# positions kept 0, then the engine's rule: mid, live at b + 2, spares 1, n_l 67 less the spare): the off
# arm hits 23.1 %, the residency arm 39.5 % over the 95 timed steps (p10..p90 over contexts 35.5..44.2),
# 96.7 % of the 23 plans at cap 24 (5.75 flips a step); P changes nothing inside 95 steps (P 0, 16, 33:
# 39.5 each). Host slots a step 264.0 -> 212.8 (first 10: 261.3, last 10: 185.9), at 0.111..0.117 ms a slot
# 5.7..6.0 ms off S1 = 47.7 ms (rig-log 09-28#glm-release). Less tau a flip x 5.75: tau 0.13 (V4.1 bp
# after swapprio, 3.40 ms / 24 flips, rig-log 09-29#swapprio-ab, by bytes) .. 0.60 (cprobe's staging c 7.8
# host slots a copy, rig-log 09-29#cprobe, on the ~70 % of a memcpy that overlaps GLM's host leg):
# +4.9..+12.4 % at the mean context; the timed prompt (ids 50000..50511) is one context, p25..p75 over the
# 24 at the band's edges +3.0..+15.3 [derived]. Break-even tau 0.99..1.04 ms a flip.
# The in-engine anchor on the same common machine (rig-log 09-30#q38res-hit, #q38res-mtp; Qwen3.8, A6000,
# plan (a), P 512): host slots a step 237 off, 229 -> 188 -> 147 on, 49 fewer at 23.6 us = 1.16 ms, the
# step 18.95 -> 18.00 ms (+3..+7 % paired: 0.55..1.24 ms), so 0.21 (-0.08..0.61) ms a step past the slots
# at 6 flips of 3.07 MB: 0.011 (<= 0.033) ms a MB; at GLM's 15.2 MB 0.17 (<= 0.50) ms a flip by bytes,
# 0.37..0.41 with the host leg's share of the step (q38 ~0.30, GLM 0.65..0.72) [derived].
# The replay's spread over contexts (35.5..44.2 % hit, +-1.6 ms) is as wide as the tau band, so the ratio
# reads tau only beside the timed prompt's own hit: the arm's host slots a token (BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1,
# which tools/ref/depth-glm5next.sh drops today: it keeps only plan|load|capture|fed|step 0|time prompt
# lines), or a route trace of ids 50000..50511 + 96 generated replayed through glmreplay.py.
# Staging: a plan's 24 x 15.2 MB = 365 MB against LIVE_DELAY 2 (two steps, 95 ms): 30..61 ms at one
# thread's 6..12 GB/s plus ~9 ms of window waits between jobs, none late; at 4.1 GB/s (130 GB/s over 32
# threads, swap.rs's own rate) 98 ms, the last job due at the landing: wait_us 0..3,000 there [derived].
# Runner (prerequisite: the `<D>@NAME=VALUE` lever arm in tools/ref/depth-glm5next.sh, depth-qwen3moe.sh's
# grammar; without it the second arm is refused, rc 64, before the lease):
#   BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=3 BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/glmres-ab.card'
#   just depth-gpu-glm5next 512 512@BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=mid-p0-s1 > <log> 2>&1
# Wall [derived]: 2 arms x (3 rounds + 1 warm-up), each a load plus 512 ids and 95 steps: 10..18 min.
kind: ab
question: at the replay's ramp (hit 23.1 -> 39.5 % over 95 steps, 5.75 flips a step), what does one
  flip's staging cost GLM's decode step on plan (a)?
term: tok/s(mean) @ n=96, depth 512, A6000, plan (a), prose ids (GLM_PROSE from GLM_PROSE_FROM),
  ctx 2048, BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=mid-p0-s1 against unset, same binary, paired by round
unit: %
predict: +3..+15
rounds: 3
sd: 0.6 % AGENTS.md 「Know the ruler」, same-binary paired ratio SD
condition: one binary, both arms in one lease, a fresh process a run (each residency run starts at the
  seed), each arm's host set preheated and its row not [cold], no [cpu-busy] or [other-busy] row; the
  residency arm prints `residency lever residency=mid-p0-s1 why=set`, a `residency host` record with
  pinned=0 and headroom_after > 0 (the churn pool 39 x 67 experts, 39.7 GB), and 96 `residency pass`
  records (pass=none, pass=prompt kept=0, 94 of pass=step kept=1) whose landed sum is 500..560 (23
  landings of 23.75); the off arm prints no residency record
decide-in: read tau = (d_slots x 0.114 - (S_off - S_on)) / flips a step, d_slots and flips the timed
  prompt's own (its host slots a token, or its route trace through glmreplay.py; the mean context's
  d_slots is 51.1 and flips 5.75);
  set plan (a)'s default to mid-p0-s1, and open the prompt-call pick (a port of V4.1's callstream pick at
  floor 32: n = 96 at 58.3 % hit, +23..+34 % [derived]) before any public row
decide-below: tau is above 0.6 ms a flip, the memcpy's host-leg interference at cprobe's size: one nsys
  window of the residency arm (where the staging thread's memcpy lands against the step port's go
  waits) before the default; wait_us over 1,000 at the landings says the staging thread runs under
  ~5 GB/s, and LIVE_DELAY 3 or a second staging thread comes first; the rule levers that price it out are the knee preset (1.3..1.5 flips a
  step, plateau +30..+33 % at any tau) and a staging that pauses outside the window
decide-above: tau is under 0.13 or the held-out prompt routes more locally than the router set's windows:
  take the n = 512 row with BLOOMERY_GEN_WARM=256 (replay +27..+39 % at P 0) before the default decision
